WEBVTT

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.370
Kokone, you once said of Musashino, where you live,

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:33.830
it’s flat, all the way to the horizon.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.350
I think I understand what you meant back then, Alpha.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:10.730
When I ride around here …

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:43.880
… It’s as though a part of my body I’ve never used before …

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:47.140
… is opening up; I get that kind of feeling.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:35.950
You see that body of water?

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:40.860
It’s the edge of a winding valley,

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:43.080
where seawater flowed in.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:52.850
I always come here by myself.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:55.290
When I’m here,

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:59.820
I think about various things, or nothing at all.

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:06.820
Alpha,

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:12.300
we’re made up of sounds and scents,

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:15.100
and not in the figurative sense.

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:18.900
I know.

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:52.920
This café … is getting old and run down, isn’t it?

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:00.210
Paint, huh …?

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:02.850
Paint is expensive though …

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:20.170
Owner …

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:25.260
The customers aren’t coming …

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:43.500
It’s time for the evening weather forecast.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:48.460
I am flying above the center of typhoon Mei Hua.

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:06.210
We, the reporters at Hamamatsu Weather Attack,

00:11:06.210 --> 00:11:09.090
will bring you information on this typhoon faster than anyone else.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:13.110
According to the weather meter we dipped below,

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:17.010
the presure at the center is 905 hectopascals …

00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:20.380
The wind speed is 10 meters per second …

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:32.780
… speed of… that is all for…

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:04.740
Oji-san!

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:14.310
Just in case … why don’t you bring just your valuables and stay at my gas station?

00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:20.610
Umm … me?

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:21.790
That’s right.

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:23.920
Yes.

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:25.470
Well, I’m gonna go take care of my house.

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:28.760
Thank you so much.

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:58.980
My house … I wonder if it’s all right?

00:18:03.370 --> 00:18:06.560
The windows … they might break.

00:18:07.780 --> 00:18:08.920
And the shutters …

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:11.900
Ah! I left the sign outside!

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:26.730
I’m starting to get worried!

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.760
I hope the typhoon goes away soon.

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:42.770
Typhoon Mei Hua, which landed from the Shounan area,

00:19:42.770 --> 00:19:44.890
passed over the plains …

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:47.410
and through the nation of Ibaragi, into Kashimanada.

00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:50.860
There seems to be substantial damage in all areas,

00:19:50.860 --> 00:19:52.960
but we don’t have the details yet.

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:55.940
During this typhoon, our team …

00:23:00.110 --> 00:23:01.290
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:23:20.120 --> 00:23:21.610
This isn’t bad.

00:23:27.650 --> 00:23:28.400
My café …

00:23:29.820 --> 00:23:31.490
It put up a good fight, I think.

00:23:33.080 --> 00:23:35.740
It’s pretty worn down as it was.

00:23:44.500 --> 00:23:47.210
You were surprisingly calm that day.

00:23:49.340 --> 00:23:50.930
I was impressed.

00:23:51.930 --> 00:23:55.170
I was in a total panic until you came.

00:23:58.230 --> 00:23:59.350
For a while …

00:24:01.190 --> 00:24:01.940
It was quite …

00:24:03.980 --> 00:24:05.070
I was crying.

00:24:13.200 --> 00:24:14.200
I see.

00:24:15.410 --> 00:24:17.950
You can still keep the café going for a while,

00:24:18.410 --> 00:24:19.450
as long as it’s sunny.

00:24:20.350 --> 00:24:23.460
Um, how has Takahiro been?

00:24:24.040 --> 00:24:24.750
Ever since then …

00:24:26.340 --> 00:24:29.370
Well, it looks like he took it pretty hard.

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:33.590
To have the scenery he grew up with disappear like that,

00:24:33.930 --> 00:24:35.550
it must have been a first for Taka.

00:24:41.440 --> 00:24:45.650
I think … I’ll be away for a bit.

00:24:46.110 --> 00:24:47.230
Gonna find a job elsewhere?

00:24:47.890 --> 00:24:49.140
Well, kind of.

00:24:51.030 --> 00:24:52.670
I want to see things,

00:24:53.240 --> 00:24:55.330
take a break from routine.

00:24:55.780 --> 00:24:57.280
I think I’ll wander around.

00:24:57.530 --> 00:24:58.640
I see.

00:24:59.410 --> 00:25:01.580
Well, be careful while you wander around.

00:25:02.040 --> 00:25:02.670
Yeah.

00:25:05.000 --> 00:25:05.790
And …

00:25:08.000 --> 00:25:09.470
Someday, I’ll definitely …

00:25:10.300 --> 00:25:11.570
rebuild my café!

00:25:17.220 --> 00:25:18.530
Would you like another cup?

00:25:19.720 --> 00:25:21.310
Yeah, I’ll have one more.

00:25:33.350 --> 00:25:36.780
Alpha, aren’t you taking the scooter?

00:25:37.410 --> 00:25:41.500
No. There might not be gas stations everywhere I go.

00:25:43.040 --> 00:25:48.950
So I thought I’d ask you to hold on to the scooter until I come back.

00:25:51.510 --> 00:25:53.760
I’m not sure if I can … ride it.

00:25:54.420 --> 00:25:55.630
I think it’ll be easy for you.

00:25:56.800 --> 00:25:59.640
You’re about as big as I am now.

00:26:00.560 --> 00:26:01.330
See?

00:26:03.060 --> 00:26:06.560
Next time we meet, you’ll probably be taller.

00:26:08.860 --> 00:26:11.040
I’ll drop by later to ask you how to ride it.

00:26:28.580 --> 00:26:29.330
Wha …

00:26:31.210 --> 00:26:32.050
Sorry.

00:26:34.490 --> 00:26:35.860
Just let me …

00:26:36.680 --> 00:26:37.750
… awhile.

00:31:03.220 --> 00:31:04.030
Takahiro!

00:31:06.550 --> 00:31:07.780
Oh, Makki.

00:31:08.150 --> 00:31:08.940
Hey.

00:31:12.960 --> 00:31:14.190
Want some coffee?

00:31:14.190 --> 00:31:14.610
Sure!

00:31:15.250 --> 00:31:15.710
Here.

00:31:16.730 --> 00:31:19.370
What? Your leftovers?

00:31:23.800 --> 00:31:24.680
Shopping?

00:31:26.900 --> 00:31:29.180
Yeah, and look!

00:31:30.530 --> 00:31:31.180
Let’s swim.

00:31:34.140 --> 00:31:35.780
It must be cold now.

00:31:35.780 --> 00:31:37.010
No problem!

00:31:40.590 --> 00:31:41.430
Takahiro.

00:31:43.650 --> 00:31:46.200
Are you worried about Alpha-san?

00:31:52.290 --> 00:31:53.540
Just a little.
